@host = http://localhost:5176

# Sign in first, then every request below carries the token. In VS Code's REST Client and
# Rider, {{login.response.body.token}} reads it straight off the named request above.
@email = you@example.com
@password = ChangeMe123
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}
@adminKey = local-operator-key

### Create an account
# @name register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Sign in — run this before anything below
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Who am I
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Health + active AI provider
GET {{host}}/api/health

### Certifications with domain weights and bank counts
GET {{host}}/api/certifications

### Generate questions (falls back to the template bank when Ai:Provider is Offline)
POST {{host}}/api/questions/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "certificationCode": "AIF-C01",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "count": 5,
  "topicHint": "Amazon Bedrock guardrails and inference parameters"
}

### Browse the question bank
GET {{host}}/api/questions?certificationCode=AIF-C01&take=10

### Start a 10-question practice set
POST {{host}}/api/exams
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "certificationCode": "AIF-C01",
  "mode": "Practice",
  "questionCount": 10
}

### Answer a question (replace both ids with values from the session above)
POST {{host}}/api/exams/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/answers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "questionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "selectedLabels": ["A"],
  "secondsSpent": 42
}

### Score the session (idempotent)
POST {{host}}/api/exams/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Completed sessions
GET {{host}}/api/exams/history?certificationCode=AIF-C01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ML.NET readiness projection
GET {{host}}/api/insights/AIF-C01/readiness
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### An administrator key alone is NOT enough: this must answer 401, not 404.
# The admin filter and [Authorize] are separate gates, and the order they run in is not
# guaranteed by reading the code - so it is pinned here as a request you can actually run.
DELETE {{host}}/api/questions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### The same call with both: an account AND the operator key.
DELETE {{host}}/api/questions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
